WEBVTT

00:06.840 --> 00:08.842
[fireworks exploding]

00:18.977 --> 00:23.314
[computer over PA] All surviving players
will be presented with two choices.

00:23.398 --> 00:28.319
Players must now decide whether to accept
permanent residency in this country,

00:28.403 --> 00:30.280
or decline it.

00:36.953 --> 00:38.246
I decline.

00:41.374 --> 00:43.668
I'm choosing not to stay here.

00:45.045 --> 00:46.296
Same for me.

00:50.091 --> 00:51.676
I don't want it.

00:52.969 --> 00:57.599
PERMANENT RESIDENCE IN THIS LAND
ACCEPT / DO NOT ACCEPT

00:57.682 --> 00:59.684
[suspenseful music playing]

01:02.604 --> 01:04.689
I accept. Naturally.

01:05.940 --> 01:08.068
I'll gladly accept it as well.

01:11.321 --> 01:14.365
There's still infinite potential
in this place.

01:31.716 --> 01:33.051
[music fades]

01:33.134 --> 01:35.720
[Arisu] I saw… a red light.

01:38.014 --> 01:39.641
I figured…

01:41.267 --> 01:45.897
I thought it was fireworks.
I didn't pay them much attention.

01:47.357 --> 01:51.611
So my friends and I…
kept hiding in the bathroom for a while.

01:52.487 --> 01:55.490
It's… pretty stupid, I guess.

01:55.573 --> 01:57.033
But we hid there.

01:59.077 --> 02:03.164
Then, everything…
became very quiet outside.

02:06.751 --> 02:10.171
I don't remember anything else. That's it.

02:13.216 --> 02:14.843
That's when you went into cardiac arrest.

02:14.926 --> 02:17.345
Because of the meteorite
and the explosion, correct?

02:18.638 --> 02:19.639
Yeah.

02:21.057 --> 02:24.644
Do you remember anything after that?
Anything at all come to mind?

02:32.235 --> 02:33.903
No, I'm sorry. I don't.

02:36.781 --> 02:41.161
After the explosion occurred,
can you remember if you were dreaming?

02:42.829 --> 02:43.872
Dreaming?

02:45.832 --> 02:47.041
About games?

02:49.377 --> 02:51.880
- Games?
- [man 2] Yes, games.

02:52.881 --> 02:54.382
Your life on the line.

02:55.133 --> 02:56.593
Does that ring a bell?

03:07.478 --> 03:08.897
Uh… no.

03:10.982 --> 03:12.609
[man 2] You didn't dream about games?

03:14.360 --> 03:15.528
Uh… no, but…

03:17.113 --> 03:18.031
But what?

03:21.326 --> 03:24.037
I feel like I did dream,
but I was on a journey.

03:26.039 --> 03:26.915
Tell me more.

03:29.459 --> 03:31.544
Like I went off traveling

03:32.420 --> 03:34.464
to some far-off place.

03:38.176 --> 03:40.303
[faint crackling]

03:44.641 --> 03:47.560
All right, that's enough for today.
You're free to go.

03:47.644 --> 03:49.103
Thanks for your time.

03:50.396 --> 03:54.692
Matsuyama, we have to be careful.
The process is delicate.

03:54.776 --> 03:57.278
We run the risk
of implanting false memories.

03:57.362 --> 03:58.821
We just have to try to be patient.

03:58.905 --> 04:01.282
That's multiple survivors
who have mentioned games.

04:01.366 --> 04:03.243
It's possible
those memories aren't accurate.

04:03.326 --> 04:05.036
And he mentioned fireworks.

04:05.119 --> 04:07.664
That's not the first time
we've heard it described that way.

04:07.747 --> 04:09.916
That was probably the meteorite.

04:11.417 --> 04:14.712
Deny it all you want.
They all saw the same thing.

04:15.213 --> 04:17.215
[tense music playing]

04:20.635 --> 04:21.886
[sighs]

04:24.931 --> 04:28.643
[man 3] I still can't believe a genius
like him is researching the afterlife.

04:28.726 --> 04:29.769
He's finished.

04:30.436 --> 04:32.605
[man 1] He's a different man now,
that's for sure.

04:32.689 --> 04:35.233
[man 3] The Shibuya meteorite
changed everyone.

04:35.316 --> 04:36.526
[man 1] No, not that.

04:36.609 --> 04:38.569
It's been five years.

04:38.653 --> 04:40.405
A student of his died. Accident.

04:40.905 --> 04:44.117
- Oh. I didn't know.
- [indistinct voices on monitors]

04:45.618 --> 04:49.205
[woman sobbing]

04:49.289 --> 04:51.165
There was nothing I could do.

04:51.249 --> 04:53.960
If you could share your recollection
of the Shibuya meteorite incident.

04:54.043 --> 04:56.379
- I'm sorry, I can't.
- [man 4] Anything you remember.

04:56.462 --> 04:58.339
[sobbing]

04:58.423 --> 05:00.091
I'm so sorry.

05:01.259 --> 05:02.969
[indistinct voices continue]

05:03.845 --> 05:05.847
[ominous music playing]

05:25.283 --> 05:26.909
[music stops]

05:31.372 --> 05:33.374
- [man 1] The main hall is that way.
- [Arisu] Thanks.

05:33.458 --> 05:35.251
- [man 1] You're welcome.
- [Arisu] Thank you.

05:35.335 --> 05:36.377
[Matsuyama] Hello there.

05:39.297 --> 05:43.634
That dream you mentioned about a journey…
I found it very interesting.

05:43.718 --> 05:46.054
- You did?
- I would love to hear more about it.

05:46.137 --> 05:47.013
[Arisu] Huh.

05:47.096 --> 05:50.016
If you remember anything,
I'd appreciate you contacting me.

05:50.099 --> 05:51.642
Okay. I will.

05:53.061 --> 05:55.396
Anything at all, even if it seems silly.

05:56.856 --> 05:58.358
What do you mean, "silly"?

05:58.441 --> 06:01.736
Like, even if you think
no one else would believe you.

06:02.779 --> 06:04.072
That sort of thing.

06:05.990 --> 06:07.992
[suspenseful music playing]

06:09.369 --> 06:10.870
[Matsuyama] It's just down here.

06:18.711 --> 06:19.545
Arisu!

06:21.047 --> 06:23.716
[Arisu] Hey!
Hope you haven't been waiting too long.

06:24.509 --> 06:25.885
Hey, you must be tired.

06:25.968 --> 06:27.595
[Arisu] No, I'm okay. Are you good?

06:35.478 --> 06:37.563
Oh, sorry. Uh, this is my wife.

06:39.440 --> 06:40.691
This is Mr. Matsuyama.

06:40.775 --> 06:43.194
- One of the professors here.
- Oh! Good to meet you.

06:43.277 --> 06:45.530
[Arisu] My wife also had
an interview here today.

06:46.072 --> 06:48.449
[Matsuyama] So you were
also a victim of the Shibuya incident?

06:48.533 --> 06:50.743
- [Usagi] That's right.
- [Matsuyama] I see.

06:51.494 --> 06:55.164
Tell me something. Would you mind terribly
if I interviewed you next time?

06:56.624 --> 06:59.794
- Uh, okay.
- My name is Ryuji Matsuyama.

07:02.422 --> 07:05.842
ASST. PROFESSOR, DEPT. OF PSYCHOPATHOLOGY
SHUSHIKAN UNIVERSITY

07:05.925 --> 07:07.468
I'll be in touch then, miss.

07:09.679 --> 07:10.555
Okay.

07:18.146 --> 07:19.689
[Usagi] What did they ask you?

07:20.523 --> 07:23.693
All sorts of things.
About my dreams, stuff like that.

07:25.027 --> 07:27.155
[Usagi] Not that we could ever remember.

07:29.282 --> 07:32.827
Ah! This university is the bomb!

07:32.910 --> 07:34.537
Wish ours was…

07:35.746 --> 07:38.833
Have you got news to your internship
at the counseling center?

07:38.916 --> 07:40.460
Hmm… Pretty much.

07:41.002 --> 07:44.380
I think after graduate school next year,
they're gonna officially hire me on.

07:44.464 --> 07:46.299
[Usagi] Oh! [laughs]

07:46.382 --> 07:49.927
- Finally becoming a proper husband.
- Hey…

07:50.011 --> 07:52.346
[both laugh]

07:58.686 --> 08:00.229
[Ryuji] Takuma Hagio.

08:01.564 --> 08:02.815
Sumiko Murakoshi.

08:02.899 --> 08:04.358
NEAR-DEATH EXPERIENCES

08:04.442 --> 08:05.610
Saaya Ishii.

08:05.693 --> 08:07.862
ANSWERS FROM THE AFTERLIFE

08:07.945 --> 08:08.946
Shuto Aida.

08:11.157 --> 08:12.700
For this investigation,

08:12.783 --> 08:15.828
we interviewed ten people
who were in a comatose state.

08:16.996 --> 08:19.207
We heard about their experiences.

08:20.583 --> 08:22.376
And all of them…

08:22.418 --> 08:24.253
COHORT STUDY ON TOKYO METEORITE SURVIVORS

08:24.337 --> 08:26.297
…had the exact same dream.

08:28.257 --> 08:29.675
An empty city.

08:30.843 --> 08:31.969
A long journey.

08:33.137 --> 08:34.222
Games.

08:35.681 --> 08:36.933
Fireworks.

08:41.437 --> 08:42.522
[phone chimes]

08:42.605 --> 08:44.315
MESSAGE

08:44.398 --> 08:46.400
[quiet, suspenseful music playing]

08:47.818 --> 08:51.239
I CAN SEE YOUR AFTERLIFE

08:52.198 --> 08:53.616
FROM: NEAR-DEATH SUPPORT GROUP INFO

08:53.699 --> 08:55.785
THERE'S A SHADY GROUP USING GROUP HYPNOSIS

08:55.868 --> 08:57.245
TELL ME MORE. I'LL PAY 100 COINS

08:57.328 --> 08:58.663
DEAL. ASK "HIM" FOR DETAILS

08:58.746 --> 09:00.122
MR. LORD
VIEW PROFILE

09:00.206 --> 09:02.208
100 COINS
COINS SENT

09:03.543 --> 09:08.214
MR. R, I FOUND A LEAD
THAT MAY INTEREST YOU

09:08.297 --> 09:10.299
[machinery whirring]

09:35.783 --> 09:39.787
[man 1] Whoa. They really
fixed up Shibuya fast, didn't they?

09:39.870 --> 09:41.372
[man 2] It's crazy.

09:41.872 --> 09:43.040
[man 1] Yeah, it's wild.

09:43.124 --> 09:44.458
[girl 1] Yay!

09:44.542 --> 09:46.919
[girl 2] What is that? Is that what you…

09:48.754 --> 09:50.256
Oh, yeah.

09:53.593 --> 09:55.595
[reversing alarm beeping]

09:57.638 --> 09:59.015
[man 3] This way, please.

10:05.271 --> 10:07.273
[suspenseful music continues]

10:52.068 --> 10:53.944
Are you… Mr. R?

10:54.028 --> 10:55.529
[music fades]

10:56.989 --> 10:57.990
Yeah.

10:58.491 --> 10:59.617
I am.

11:11.504 --> 11:12.713
[woman] So, um,

11:14.006 --> 11:15.383
this seminar.

11:16.092 --> 11:18.386
You're hoping to attend as well, are you?

11:20.012 --> 11:20.971
Yes.

11:21.889 --> 11:23.557
Could you invite me to it?

11:24.058 --> 11:26.560
- I heard that getting a referral is tough…
- [glass clinks]

11:27.895 --> 11:30.189
Let me know when you're ready to order.

11:30.981 --> 11:33.234
- Tea, please.
- And the same for me.

11:34.026 --> 11:35.069
[server] Right away.

11:37.988 --> 11:39.699
So, Mr. R.

11:39.782 --> 11:41.992
I don't recommend participating.

11:43.077 --> 11:44.328
[shakily] But you'll

11:45.496 --> 11:47.581
understand when you do get there.

11:48.082 --> 11:49.417
You'll know it's the real thing.

11:52.503 --> 11:54.839
What kind of experiences did you have?

11:58.300 --> 12:00.386
We do… strange things.

12:00.886 --> 12:02.596
[low, unsettling music playing]

12:02.680 --> 12:06.183
What do you mean by "strange"?
What kind of things?

12:09.645 --> 12:10.771
Games.

12:15.067 --> 12:16.068
Games?

12:17.486 --> 12:19.113
Yes, games.

12:19.613 --> 12:21.824
They can be… exciting.

12:23.242 --> 12:26.203
They can be… sacred too.

12:39.049 --> 12:42.887
[woman] In one week,
you will receive an invitation by email.

12:43.763 --> 12:46.724
The location of the meeting
will be specified then.

12:46.807 --> 12:48.809
[grunting]

12:51.645 --> 12:53.022
INBOX: (NO SUBJECT)

12:55.524 --> 12:57.234
[straining]

12:58.068 --> 12:59.111
[groans]

13:04.700 --> 13:06.202
[grunts]

13:07.119 --> 13:08.204
[sighs]

13:09.079 --> 13:11.081
[breathing heavily]

13:17.588 --> 13:19.423
MR. R, THANK YOU FOR YOUR INTEREST

13:19.507 --> 13:22.968
AFTER CAREFUL REVIEW,
WE HEREBY INVITE YOU TO THE "SEMINAR"

13:28.516 --> 13:31.227
TUE, OCT 14, 2024, 23:00
KŌTŌ SIDE OFFICE

13:31.310 --> 13:34.647
WE LOOK FORWARD
TO YOUR ATTENDANCE, MR. R

13:44.490 --> 13:45.991
[music fades]

14:06.887 --> 14:08.681
[elevator chimes]

14:29.451 --> 14:31.287
[low, suspenseful music playing]

15:29.970 --> 15:31.472
[music fades]

15:31.555 --> 15:33.724
[man 1] Thank you all for coming.

15:34.892 --> 15:37.519
Please. Take a seat.

15:41.565 --> 15:43.067
[music fades]

15:58.874 --> 16:00.793
Take a seat please, sir.

16:02.086 --> 16:03.420
On that chair.

16:04.171 --> 16:07.841
It would be best not to move
from the seat you've chosen.

16:23.482 --> 16:25.275
[Ryuji breathing heavily]

16:29.196 --> 16:30.406
[sighs]

16:31.448 --> 16:32.825
[grunts]

16:33.409 --> 16:35.995
Very well. Let us begin our game now.

16:37.538 --> 16:38.664
Game?

16:39.957 --> 16:43.043
I came here to have
a near-death experience.

16:43.752 --> 16:47.923
You must win this game
to participate in the journey.

16:48.924 --> 16:50.009
Journey?

16:50.801 --> 16:52.803
[quiet, ominous music playing]

16:54.179 --> 16:56.056
Now, let us begin.

16:56.682 --> 16:59.226
The game is Old Maid.

17:01.020 --> 17:03.022
[ominous music intensifies]

17:07.067 --> 17:08.777
[man 1] Please take your cards.

17:17.161 --> 17:21.665
If there are pairs of cards in your hand,
you must discard them.

17:22.332 --> 17:23.834
[woman 2] I've got a pair!

17:23.917 --> 17:25.919
[man 1] Whoever holds the Joker is
the Old Maid.

17:26.003 --> 17:29.423
And whoever holds the Joker
at the end of the game is the winner.

17:30.632 --> 17:33.260
All right, then. You, start.

17:34.595 --> 17:38.182
But be warned… when the Joker is drawn
from a player's hand,

17:38.265 --> 17:40.267
that player will be eliminated.

17:41.310 --> 17:42.519
- Wait, what?
- [power crackles]

17:42.603 --> 17:44.104
- [groans]
- [sizzling]

17:44.188 --> 17:45.230
- [thud]
- [woman 2 gasps]

17:45.314 --> 17:46.607
- [screams]
- [power crackles]

17:46.690 --> 17:48.067
[whimpers]

17:49.818 --> 17:52.071
[man 1] I thought I made myself clear.

17:52.863 --> 17:55.991
It would be best not to move
from the seat you've chosen.

17:56.992 --> 18:00.579
Because if you do…
you, too, will be eliminated.

18:01.413 --> 18:02.247
[breathing shakily]

18:02.331 --> 18:04.041
She's dead. [whimpers]

18:04.124 --> 18:05.667
[gasping]

18:05.751 --> 18:08.921
She can't be. No way.
She's just pretending, huh?

18:09.004 --> 18:11.006
[dramatic music playing]

18:13.592 --> 18:15.594
[trembling]

18:39.993 --> 18:41.078
[sighs]

18:42.121 --> 18:43.997
[whimpering softly]

18:46.250 --> 18:47.835
[moans]

19:19.992 --> 19:21.577
[woman 1 whimpering]

19:24.163 --> 19:25.164
[gasps]

19:26.081 --> 19:27.457
[power surges]

19:28.876 --> 19:30.419
[sobbing]

19:30.502 --> 19:33.463
- [sighs]
- This is starting to get interesting.

19:36.466 --> 19:38.302
[man 2 continues sobbing]

19:44.391 --> 19:45.642
[moans]

19:45.726 --> 19:47.436
- [power crackles]
- [grunts]

19:47.519 --> 19:49.062
[sizzling]

20:01.992 --> 20:03.493
[breathing heavily]

20:06.538 --> 20:09.124
[gasps] Oh my God!

20:09.208 --> 20:10.626
[power surges]

20:22.054 --> 20:23.680
[man 3 breathing shakily]

20:27.434 --> 20:31.104
There's no hope at this point, is there?
One of us will die.

20:39.613 --> 20:40.822
[whimpers]

20:49.122 --> 20:50.165
[music fades]

20:51.208 --> 20:52.876
[gasps]

20:52.960 --> 20:54.211
[wails]

20:54.294 --> 20:55.629
- [power surges]
- [grunts]

20:56.755 --> 20:58.257
[sizzling]

20:58.340 --> 21:00.342
[breathing heavily]

21:01.760 --> 21:03.428
[gasping]

21:08.809 --> 21:10.811
[lights crackling]

21:14.523 --> 21:16.483
[low, ominous music playing]

21:27.744 --> 21:29.830
[music intensifying]

21:42.301 --> 21:45.804
Welcome… to the Borderlands.

21:59.860 --> 22:01.486
[music fades]

22:02.362 --> 22:04.364
[theme music playing]

23:03.715 --> 23:05.008
[soft rustling]

23:05.092 --> 23:07.094
[woman breathing shakily]

23:14.810 --> 23:16.812
[quiet, eerie music playing]

23:17.896 --> 23:19.898
[breathing heavily]

23:35.330 --> 23:36.415
[gasps]

23:36.915 --> 23:37.999
Dad?

23:50.011 --> 23:51.346
[gasps]

24:00.856 --> 24:01.940
[gasps]

24:05.193 --> 24:06.319
[gasp echoing]

24:06.403 --> 24:08.530
- [breathing heavily]
- [music stops]

24:18.540 --> 24:19.833
Are you okay?

24:21.001 --> 24:21.960
Yeah.

24:25.046 --> 24:26.089
[sighs]

24:27.215 --> 24:29.009
[Arisu] You were having a bad dream.

24:31.178 --> 24:32.512
You sure you're okay?

24:34.306 --> 24:36.766
Yeah. I'm okay.

24:39.394 --> 24:41.062
I'll get some water.

24:44.232 --> 24:45.400
[sighs]

24:47.611 --> 24:49.321
[birdsong]

24:49.404 --> 24:51.031
[delicate music playing]

24:51.114 --> 24:54.409
YUZUHA ARISU

24:54.493 --> 24:56.661
RESIDENTIAL LEASE

24:56.745 --> 25:00.290
[Arisu] We should probably think
about buying eventually, don't you think?

25:00.373 --> 25:03.502
For that, we need to save money first.

25:03.585 --> 25:05.045
[Arisu] Right.

25:05.587 --> 25:08.256
[chuckles] We did splurge
on the wedding rings, after all.

25:09.758 --> 25:11.635
- [Arisu] True, yeah.
- [Usagi chuckles]

25:12.886 --> 25:15.222
Look. Isn't this color kind of rare?

25:15.305 --> 25:17.807
Oh yeah… I didn't mean to buy that one.

25:18.808 --> 25:20.560
[Usagi] Well, I quite like this color.

25:20.644 --> 25:22.562
- [laughs]
- [Arisu] Yeah? It's yours.

25:22.646 --> 25:24.439
- [Usagi] Really?
- [both laugh]

25:25.524 --> 25:27.234
You need help moving?

25:27.317 --> 25:30.403
[Usagi] No. I'll hire someone.
I have to work too.

25:30.904 --> 25:32.781
Arisu, will you take care of this?

25:32.864 --> 25:33.949
Mm-hmm.

25:34.574 --> 25:36.284
[Usagi] I should really get going.

25:36.868 --> 25:39.079
- [Arisu] Take care!
- See you later.

25:39.871 --> 25:40.872
[sighs]

25:42.582 --> 25:45.418
[laughs] Are you still
brushing your teeth, Arisu?

25:45.502 --> 25:48.129
- You'll be late. Hurry up!
- Mmm. Bye!

25:52.050 --> 25:53.426
- [door closes]
- [music fades]

25:53.510 --> 25:54.761
[horn blares]

25:56.096 --> 25:58.723
[reporter] In other news,
police have discovered seven bodies

25:58.807 --> 26:00.976
in an office block in Kōtō Ward, Tokyo.

26:01.059 --> 26:04.771
Police say all seven were attending
a seminar when they died.

26:05.355 --> 26:09.067
While there is some evidence to suggest
that it may have been a mass suicide,

26:09.150 --> 26:10.860
the investigation continues.

26:13.488 --> 26:17.534
[man] The waterfront neighborhood
has gotten very popular with tourists.

26:17.617 --> 26:21.079
We've already seen some start to visit,
and we're expecting more weekly.

26:21.162 --> 26:23.582
Then a wide range of sizes would be best.

26:23.665 --> 26:27.210
In Shinjuku and Shibuya, larger sizes that
don't sell at other stores do sell here.

26:27.294 --> 26:28.169
- Ah! That's true!
- Yes.

26:28.253 --> 26:29.546
You know, I didn't think of that.

26:33.967 --> 26:35.552
[Arisu] Here's the referral letter.

26:35.635 --> 26:39.306
This one's from a client affected
by the disaster at Shibuya.

26:40.765 --> 26:42.601
Their PTSD has become chronic,

26:42.684 --> 26:45.353
and flashbacks to the incident
seem to be getting stronger.

26:46.229 --> 26:48.273
Right. Trauma from the meteorite.

26:49.649 --> 26:51.443
- You can show them in.
- Got it.

26:51.943 --> 26:53.486
[soft music playing]

26:53.570 --> 26:54.738
[woman] Thank you for waiting.

26:54.821 --> 26:57.907
Would you mind filling out
this questionnaire? No rush.

26:58.408 --> 27:00.619
And don't forget your name and address.

27:03.079 --> 27:05.749
Good morning. Thanks for your patience.

27:08.793 --> 27:10.337
Would you mind coming next door?

27:11.421 --> 27:13.423
[quiet, suspenseful music playing]

27:25.018 --> 27:26.853
Can I get you something to drink?

27:27.354 --> 27:29.981
There's coffee, tea… We've got options.

27:30.565 --> 27:32.651
And there's cold drinks if you'd prefer.

27:33.151 --> 27:34.152
[Ann] Arisu…

27:39.240 --> 27:40.158
We've…

27:41.326 --> 27:43.370
You and I have already met.

27:45.705 --> 27:46.748
We have?

27:47.582 --> 27:49.584
[suspenseful music continues]

28:39.300 --> 28:41.094
[Ann] I know you. I've met you.

28:41.886 --> 28:44.139
Some place very far from here.

28:46.182 --> 28:48.017
No. I don't think so.

28:49.102 --> 28:52.272
[Ann] Among those who have had
near-death experiences,

28:53.064 --> 28:55.734
there are many who said
they saw another world.

28:57.527 --> 28:59.571
But what was it they saw there?

29:00.530 --> 29:03.450
Was it hope, or did they see only despair?

29:06.536 --> 29:08.163
You must have seen it

29:09.122 --> 29:10.915
when you were near to death.

29:12.792 --> 29:15.295
You must have memories of that world.

29:20.133 --> 29:21.301
Arisu…

29:22.969 --> 29:24.804
I see you've forgotten.

29:26.431 --> 29:28.433
[buzz of voices]

29:43.448 --> 29:45.450
[music intensifying]

29:59.172 --> 30:00.381
[Ann] You don't remember.

30:01.049 --> 30:03.843
I understand you might think
I'm out of my mind.

30:04.677 --> 30:08.264
I know.
But that world between worlds exists.

30:09.015 --> 30:11.726
You and I both were there.

30:12.310 --> 30:15.104
We fought in that place, and we survived.

30:17.148 --> 30:19.359
And because we survived,

30:20.276 --> 30:22.570
we were able to return to this world.

30:52.976 --> 30:54.352
[breathing shakily]

31:07.657 --> 31:09.200
[gasping]

31:21.212 --> 31:23.214
[gasping]

31:23.298 --> 31:25.008
[sobbing]

31:27.218 --> 31:29.554
[Ann] But I can't remember everything.

31:29.637 --> 31:31.264
I want to know what happened to us.

31:31.848 --> 31:34.559
But here, there's only so much I can do.

31:35.435 --> 31:37.604
I wanted to know if we could go back.

31:39.856 --> 31:41.482
And I found a way.

31:42.400 --> 31:45.194
We can return to that world
if we choose to.

31:49.115 --> 31:51.075
If I administer a certain drug.

31:52.327 --> 31:53.536
[music fades]

31:53.620 --> 31:55.455
Thanks for your patience.

31:57.123 --> 31:58.583
Please, take a seat.

32:02.003 --> 32:03.963
[buzz of voices]

32:04.047 --> 32:05.882
[breathing unsteadily]

32:16.392 --> 32:17.727
[gasps]

32:24.025 --> 32:26.027
[low, sinister music playing]

32:30.615 --> 32:32.241
[music fades]

32:39.499 --> 32:41.125
[sighs]

32:45.463 --> 32:47.340
[phone buzzing]

32:49.467 --> 32:51.886
INCOMING CALL
YUZUHA USAGI

32:53.846 --> 32:55.223
You done at work?

32:56.307 --> 32:57.308
Arisu…

32:57.934 --> 32:59.352
Will I see you tonight?

32:59.852 --> 33:01.354
- [sighs]
- [Usagi sobbing]

33:04.023 --> 33:05.525
Hey, Usagi.

33:06.442 --> 33:07.527
Where are you?

33:09.529 --> 33:10.822
Arisu…

33:12.532 --> 33:13.533
Huh?

33:14.575 --> 33:15.910
I'll come get you.

33:18.830 --> 33:20.832
[breathing shakily]

33:22.792 --> 33:25.044
- [Usagi crying softly]
- Usagi?

33:27.672 --> 33:29.549
I'm sorry. [gasps]

33:30.133 --> 33:31.634
- Wait. Where are--
- [call drops]

33:33.386 --> 33:35.388
[gentle, melancholy music playing]

33:42.854 --> 33:45.940
We're sorry.
The person you are trying to reach is--

33:52.321 --> 33:53.698
[panting]

34:00.997 --> 34:02.665
[doorbell rings]

34:14.844 --> 34:15.803
Usagi?

34:21.559 --> 34:22.810
- Usagi?
- [knocking]

34:24.937 --> 34:27.273
[man 1] Based on the information
we received from you,

34:27.356 --> 34:29.984
the Public Safety Division
is also looking into it.

34:30.568 --> 34:34.405
Although I will say,
we haven't found anything suspicious yet.

34:34.489 --> 34:37.742
Okay, but I called her company,
and they haven't heard from her either.

34:37.825 --> 34:41.621
Uh-huh. We did find something
that we'd like for you to see.

34:41.704 --> 34:43.748
- Show him.
- [taps keys]

34:45.041 --> 34:47.251
What we're looking at
is surveillance camera footage

34:47.335 --> 34:49.212
from the hotel where
your wife was last seen.

34:51.130 --> 34:54.425
It's a resort hotel near the waterfront.

34:54.509 --> 34:56.511
[suspenseful music playing]

34:58.971 --> 35:01.599
[man 2] Sir, do you know this man?

35:04.268 --> 35:05.353
[Arisu] Yeah.

35:05.937 --> 35:07.772
I met him a couple of weeks ago.

35:08.481 --> 35:11.109
He's an assistant professor at Shushikan.

35:11.192 --> 35:13.319
[man 1] Did your wife also know this man?

35:14.487 --> 35:18.366
We met him at the same time.
We were doing a study at the university.

35:22.495 --> 35:24.205
So you're saying he kidnapped her, then?

35:25.665 --> 35:29.210
No. There's another scenario
to consider, sir.

35:30.044 --> 35:31.963
I don't want to be indelicate,

35:32.463 --> 35:34.924
but is it at all… possible

35:35.007 --> 35:37.760
she was having an affair
with this professor?

35:38.886 --> 35:40.638
They did meet at a hotel.

35:40.721 --> 35:43.057
And you told us they were acquainted.

35:43.141 --> 35:46.102
This might be a possibility
for you to look into

35:46.185 --> 35:49.272
before filing an official
missing persons report.

35:49.772 --> 35:51.274
[music fades]

35:57.238 --> 35:59.490
[Arisu] I'm looking
for Professor Matsuyama.

35:59.574 --> 36:01.033
My wife has disappeared.

36:01.117 --> 36:03.744
And the last person
she saw was the professor.

36:03.828 --> 36:04.745
[gasps]

36:04.829 --> 36:06.706
Professor Matsuyama's also gone.

36:06.789 --> 36:08.916
We lost contact with him
a couple days ago.

36:09.500 --> 36:10.459
What?

36:14.672 --> 36:17.967
[woman] The professor was absorbed
in very unusual research.

36:18.467 --> 36:21.387
Near-death experiences,
the afterlife, things like that.

36:21.470 --> 36:23.890
But he's not the type
to just take leave without notice.

36:23.973 --> 36:26.642
So I wondered if something
had happened to him.

36:29.729 --> 36:31.731
[quiet, eerie music playing]

36:32.481 --> 36:33.566
[woman gasps]

36:34.650 --> 36:38.487
He was also investigating
various occult gatherings recently.

36:39.697 --> 36:41.115
If I'm honest, I was getting worried.

36:41.199 --> 36:42.116
MASS SUICIDES AND CULTS

36:42.200 --> 36:43.242
NEAR-DEATH EXPERIENCES

36:43.326 --> 36:45.786
Was your wife involved with a cult?

36:56.631 --> 37:00.343
SHIGENORI USAGI COMMITS SUICIDE
FOLLOWING RUMORS OF STAGED CLIMB?

37:03.930 --> 37:06.140
YUZUHA ARISU

37:12.605 --> 37:15.650
YUZUHA ARISU: INTERVIEW

37:16.651 --> 37:18.361
[Ryuji] Do you have vivid dreams?

37:22.240 --> 37:24.033
Pretty often, actually.

37:25.660 --> 37:27.787
[Ryuji] What kind of dreams do you have?

37:27.870 --> 37:30.414
Give me as much detail
as you can remember.

37:36.754 --> 37:39.882
[Usagi] I have the same dream,
over and over.

37:41.634 --> 37:42.885
[Ryuji] This dream…

37:43.427 --> 37:45.221
Is it more of a nightmare?

37:48.933 --> 37:50.518
It's… [sighs]

37:54.897 --> 37:57.066
My father commit suicide.

37:58.276 --> 38:00.319
- [sighs]
- [Ryuji] I see.

38:01.028 --> 38:03.531
Was there any bad blood between
you and your father?

38:03.614 --> 38:05.283
Any unresolved issues?

38:05.783 --> 38:07.451
Absolutely not.

38:07.535 --> 38:09.495
[quiet, tense music playing]

38:09.578 --> 38:11.539
My dad was wonderful.

38:13.791 --> 38:15.334
[Ryuji] Is it possible

38:16.043 --> 38:18.879
you feel like you didn't get
to properly say goodbye?

38:20.089 --> 38:22.550
Or is there something
you regret not telling him?

38:27.972 --> 38:28.973
[inhales]

38:29.056 --> 38:30.599
[Ryuji] Don't push yourself.

38:30.683 --> 38:31.600
[sighs]

38:33.811 --> 38:35.980
[Usagi] It's all right.
Please listen to me.

38:36.689 --> 38:39.483
This is something
I can't tell anyone else.

38:40.776 --> 38:42.403
[Ryuji] Not even your husband?

38:45.531 --> 38:46.907
I can't tell him.

38:47.575 --> 38:49.160
Not even now.

38:52.038 --> 38:55.124
I met my husband, we got married…

38:55.833 --> 38:59.003
I should be moving forward
with him in life, you know?

39:01.088 --> 39:03.966
But I can't stop thinking about my father.

39:10.264 --> 39:12.266
[suspenseful music continues]

39:13.934 --> 39:15.561
[Usagi] When I dream,

39:16.937 --> 39:18.606
I can feel him.

39:18.689 --> 39:20.024
My father's presence.

39:20.107 --> 39:22.777
As if he were still living and breathing.

39:26.655 --> 39:29.158
And even if he dies in my dream,

39:30.117 --> 39:31.952
even if it hurts…

39:33.662 --> 39:34.538
[sobs]

39:34.622 --> 39:37.375
Even if I have to watch
him die over and over…

39:38.167 --> 39:40.169
If my dad is in my dreams…

39:40.920 --> 39:41.962
[sighs]

39:51.222 --> 39:52.556
[music fades]

39:53.432 --> 39:55.726
Then, even if they're nightmares…

39:58.145 --> 39:59.855
that's where I wanna go.

40:14.537 --> 40:16.747
[ominous music playing]

40:16.831 --> 40:17.915
[gasps]

40:20.292 --> 40:23.921
[Banda] It's you. The player
who helped to beat every single game.

40:24.004 --> 40:25.131
[music fades]

40:25.214 --> 40:28.134
[Banda] I became a citizen thanks to you.

40:35.516 --> 40:37.726
I was hoping I'd meet you some day.

40:38.894 --> 40:41.021
Won't you come back with me?

40:41.105 --> 40:43.149
See that beautiful place again?

40:44.567 --> 40:46.569
[suspenseful music playing]

40:51.490 --> 40:53.742
Pretty soon, you'll remember everything.

40:54.243 --> 40:57.079
And when you do,
you'll return to that world.

41:00.708 --> 41:02.376
Let's play a new game.

41:07.465 --> 41:11.218
And by the way, your precious wife
will also be playing in the games.

41:13.012 --> 41:14.221
The new games.

41:18.684 --> 41:19.685
Let's have some fun.

41:21.353 --> 41:22.730
[chuckles]

41:27.359 --> 41:28.986
[music fades]

41:42.208 --> 41:43.125
Huh?

41:46.754 --> 41:48.714
[foreboding music playing]

41:52.092 --> 41:53.719
[phone buzzing]

41:59.767 --> 42:02.603
- [Arisu] How is she? What happened?
- She's currently in a coma.

42:02.686 --> 42:05.814
But I wouldn't be surprised
if she went into cardiac arrest.

42:05.898 --> 42:09.401
[man 2] We don't know much yet.
No signs of struggle or resistance.

42:09.485 --> 42:11.028
At least, not that we've found.

42:11.111 --> 42:12.655
But the doctor's report suggests

42:12.738 --> 42:15.574
the man who she was with made her
consume some sort of drug.

42:15.658 --> 42:18.744
- [Arisu] What kind of drug?
- [man 2] Might've been attempted suicide.

42:19.995 --> 42:21.956
[man 3] Doctor. They're here.

42:23.874 --> 42:26.126
- [doctor] You her husband?
- [Arisu] Yes.

42:26.669 --> 42:28.504
[doctor] I don't want
to overwhelm you, sir,

42:28.587 --> 42:31.298
but we performed standard
blood tests on your wife.

42:32.049 --> 42:34.093
And it would seem that she is pregnant.

42:34.927 --> 42:35.886
What?

42:35.970 --> 42:39.557
It's still in the very early stages.
It wouldn't even have a heartbeat yet.

42:40.140 --> 42:42.726
Your wife may not have even known herself.

42:43.811 --> 42:44.812
Come with me.

42:45.688 --> 42:47.106
[door opens]

42:49.066 --> 42:50.901
[monitor bleeping steadily]

43:10.713 --> 43:12.590
Usagi…

43:14.550 --> 43:18.012
[man 2] Sir, this is the man we found
alongside her, comatose as well.

43:18.929 --> 43:20.556
Would you mind taking a look?

43:23.851 --> 43:25.394
[quiet, unsettling music playing]

43:32.443 --> 43:33.902
[man 3] You know him, don't you?

43:34.778 --> 43:37.698
Maybe we could… have a quick word?

43:45.831 --> 43:47.124
[music fades]

43:47.207 --> 43:51.712
[man 2] Tell us, are you aware
of the recent mass suicides?

43:51.795 --> 43:53.339
The ones in Tokyo?

43:54.214 --> 43:55.341
[Arisu] Not really.

43:56.133 --> 43:59.803
So, what then?
You're saying this guy took my wife

43:59.887 --> 44:02.514
and got caught up
in one of those mass suicide attempts?

44:02.598 --> 44:06.602
This man had some apparent connection
to those "seminars."

44:06.685 --> 44:09.813
We've confirmed their movements
from the hotel.

44:10.481 --> 44:14.735
First off, she was taken
to the university where the man worked.

44:14.818 --> 44:19.782
After that, they went together straight
to the building where they were found.

44:20.532 --> 44:22.117
So what we're saying

44:22.826 --> 44:25.496
is that there's a possibility
your wife was caught up in this.

44:29.041 --> 44:31.001
I told you she might've been kidnapped.

44:32.086 --> 44:35.422
I told you!
I told you this before, didn't I?

44:36.423 --> 44:38.092
I know. I'm sorry.

44:38.759 --> 44:42.721
But without evidence of a crime,
we can only do so much, sir.

44:43.806 --> 44:45.516
[breathing shakily]

44:49.019 --> 44:51.563
[sighs] Can we ask you, sir…

44:53.273 --> 44:56.068
Would you mind checking
your wife's belongings for us?

44:56.151 --> 44:57.361
Could you get that?

45:00.698 --> 45:02.616
Uh… come take a look.

45:03.325 --> 45:05.244
This is what your wife had on her.

45:05.744 --> 45:07.621
Is there anything out of place?

45:24.805 --> 45:26.306
[inhales]

45:43.073 --> 45:44.199
[sighs]

45:47.327 --> 45:49.329
[ominous music playing]

45:59.548 --> 46:00.549
[man 3] Well?

46:01.800 --> 46:03.427
Anything different, sir?

46:03.927 --> 46:07.681
And by the way, your precious wife
will also be playing in the games.

46:11.935 --> 46:13.270
Uh… Uh-uh.

46:15.355 --> 46:17.274
What about that joker card?

46:17.775 --> 46:21.236
The man who was with her,
Matsuyama, he had one just like it.

46:28.452 --> 46:30.162
[Ryuji] Even if it seems silly.

46:31.789 --> 46:33.081
What do you mean, "silly"?

46:33.165 --> 46:36.376
Like, even if you think
no one else would believe you.

46:36.460 --> 46:38.003
No. I don't think so.

46:38.086 --> 46:40.297
[Ann] That world between worlds exists.

46:45.135 --> 46:46.470
[music fades]

46:48.889 --> 46:51.809
TAKINOGAWA SANATORIUM

46:53.227 --> 46:56.605
[child] A-choo-choo, choo-choo, choo-choo.

46:56.688 --> 46:59.733
Choo-choo-choo…

46:59.817 --> 47:01.860
- [nurse] This way, please.
- Choo-choo…

47:02.528 --> 47:04.571
Choo-choo! Choo-choo-choo…

47:04.655 --> 47:06.323
[loud ticking]

47:07.574 --> 47:08.784
[faint birdsong]

47:12.663 --> 47:13.997
[Arisu] My wife, she's

47:14.665 --> 47:16.416
in a coma in the hospital.

47:17.543 --> 47:18.794
And she's pregnant.

47:19.920 --> 47:22.631
But her pulse is so weak, it's

47:23.465 --> 47:25.008
just a matter of time.

47:27.636 --> 47:31.348
There was a man.
He gave me one of these Jokers.

47:34.268 --> 47:36.562
You said we had been to that other world.

47:37.187 --> 47:38.689
We fought and lived.

47:38.772 --> 47:41.483
And that's how
we returned to this world, isn't it?

47:43.235 --> 47:46.113
The man who gave me this
said something… similar.

47:47.406 --> 47:50.868
He might have her. My wife, my child.

47:50.951 --> 47:52.995
He might take them to that place.

47:55.455 --> 47:57.416
I know it might not make much sense.

47:58.834 --> 48:02.963
But please, if there's a way
to bring my wife back here,

48:03.463 --> 48:04.631
I'll do anything.

48:05.257 --> 48:06.383
Help me, Ann.

48:11.680 --> 48:13.181
[breathing shakily]

48:14.933 --> 48:15.809
Just two.

48:16.894 --> 48:17.811
Huh?

48:18.312 --> 48:20.022
[quiet, tense music playing]

48:20.105 --> 48:23.191
From the time
that a person's heart stops beating

48:23.692 --> 48:26.153
but before they actually die,

48:26.236 --> 48:28.280
two minutes pass
where they're between life and death.

48:28.947 --> 48:33.493
It varies from person to person a bit,
but for most it's about two minutes or so.

48:34.578 --> 48:37.956
And then, you enter a special state,
which I believe

48:38.540 --> 48:40.292
is a collective unconsciousness.

48:40.375 --> 48:42.085
We experienced that world.

48:42.669 --> 48:44.046
So if you go

48:44.671 --> 48:47.299
and get her back safely
within two minutes,

48:48.926 --> 48:51.136
she should be able to return.

48:53.388 --> 48:54.806
Two minutes?

48:56.433 --> 48:58.644
When we were in that place before,

48:59.144 --> 49:01.146
our experience spanned days.

49:01.647 --> 49:03.106
But our hearts

49:03.732 --> 49:06.693
were only stopped
for a minute in the real world.

49:07.194 --> 49:08.612
Does that make sense?

49:09.363 --> 49:11.698
In the real world, time passes one way.

49:11.782 --> 49:14.785
But in this collective unconsciousness
that we experienced,

49:14.868 --> 49:16.411
time flows differently.

49:17.412 --> 49:18.789
It's two minutes.

49:19.373 --> 49:21.291
It's barely a moment for you.

49:21.833 --> 49:23.669
There, you might fight a war.

49:27.839 --> 49:29.508
Are you serious about this?

49:30.425 --> 49:33.053
You came to me
because you do believe, don't you?

49:37.015 --> 49:39.101
But this is all hypothetical, really.

49:39.685 --> 49:40.769
I can't

49:41.520 --> 49:43.397
say for sure that you'll come back.

49:43.981 --> 49:45.732
What if I'm trapped there?

49:47.526 --> 49:49.152
You'll die, obviously.

49:49.861 --> 49:51.530
And they'll jail me for life.

49:52.030 --> 49:54.491
Assisted suicide or murder charges.

49:57.869 --> 49:59.579
- [phone buzzing]
- [Arisu gasps]

50:06.753 --> 50:07.921
[gasps] Hello?

50:10.757 --> 50:11.675
I see.

50:17.931 --> 50:19.433
[Ann] She's out of time.

50:27.149 --> 50:28.900
I don't care what happens to me.

50:30.736 --> 50:33.071
If there's a chance I can save Usagi,

50:33.780 --> 50:35.323
I'll do whatever it takes.

50:36.283 --> 50:38.285
[music swells]

50:51.131 --> 50:52.507
INSULINACT

50:56.094 --> 50:57.429
You're gonna use that?

50:57.929 --> 50:59.723
Yes, it'll stop your heart.

51:00.223 --> 51:01.308
For a time.

51:01.391 --> 51:02.851
It'll stop my heart?

51:02.934 --> 51:05.479
There's no time to second-guess. You in?

51:13.987 --> 51:15.113
Two minutes.

51:16.156 --> 51:17.074
Uh-huh.

51:24.372 --> 51:25.916
[breathing shakily]

51:29.419 --> 51:30.670
[music fades]

51:32.631 --> 51:33.924
Can you feel anything?

51:34.007 --> 51:35.884
I don't think it worked. [gasps]

51:38.929 --> 51:40.972
We're running out of time, Ann!

51:41.932 --> 51:43.892
[breathing heavily]

51:47.979 --> 51:49.314
The clock's stop--

51:50.190 --> 51:51.983
[silence]

52:01.618 --> 52:02.577
Ann?

52:07.541 --> 52:08.583
Ann?

53:00.844 --> 53:02.846
[quiet, suspenseful music playing]

53:17.527 --> 53:20.947
PROCEED 15 KM SOUTH-SOUTHEAST
THE "GAME" STARTS AT SUNDOWN

54:20.048 --> 54:21.049
Usagi?

54:23.218 --> 54:30.225
THE "GAME" ARENA IS 6 KM AHEAD

54:51.371 --> 54:53.581
"GAME" ARENA AHEAD

54:56.418 --> 54:57.752
[music fades]

55:02.674 --> 55:04.551
[quiet, tense music playing]

55:29.659 --> 55:31.661
[music intensifies]

56:01.483 --> 56:03.485
[music intensifies]

56:05.779 --> 56:07.113
[bell chimes]

56:28.593 --> 56:30.095
[music fades]

56:32.263 --> 56:34.557
FRIED NOODLES

56:34.641 --> 56:36.101
COTTON CANDY

